[step] Required SB443-IN groove-capture interface. Each rail projects 0.700 mm into the 6.650 mm slot and is 0.600 mm along Y. The full-tolerance common groove interval is only 0.8382 mm (1.8542–2.6924 mm behind the pole); the rail occupies 2.000–2.600 mm, and its tips leave 0.1104 mm against the largest groove neck. Mechanically keyed DP420 bedding fills the actual axial allowance. magnet-geometry.json binds the supplier envelope, front loading and positive keyed retention in the actual final host. Printed rail/key strength and repeated removal remain unqualified.
alternatives: A 3 mm rail cannot enter this purchased groove. Extending it along Y consumes supplier groove air; increasing X engagement consumes the worst-neck clearance. Removing it leaves adhesion as the axial restraint. A different magnet or separate bolted retainer changes the purchased interface or adds factory parts and operations.
file: hardware/printed-parts/enclosure/enclosure/enclosure-pump-cartridge.step
