[sliver] Specific mating magnet guard: these 1.350 mm strips are its exposed axial projection from Y82.265 to Y83.615, with ordinary 3 mm side/floor stock around the column and 0.250 mm running air in the fixed recess. The pole remains 0.650 mm ahead of the guard. This face width is the required insertion overlap, rather than a 1.350 mm wall section. magnet-geometry.json reads the complete source stock, actual host, supplier loading and swept mating guard.
alternatives: Making the projection 3 mm would pass the bare pole plane and prevent face contact. Removing it exposes the full 2 mm magnet projection; shortening it reduces insertion protection. A longer matching recess consumes the fixed housing stock ahead of its side keys. Keep the specified overlap and qualify printed fit, angled insertion and edge chipping.
