[ceiling] Lower guide surface of each 1.350 mm projecting magnet guard. The full floor above it retains 3 mm beneath the stack and cured keys; its matching fixed-wall recess provides 0.250 mm running clearance. The exposed +Y underside has an open Tree (auto)/Default support-removal route before magnet installation. Printed finish, cleanup and floor strength remain unqualified.
alternatives: A 45° cut inside this envelope spends the required 3 mm floor at the proud edge. An additive downward wedge preserves the floor but requires a larger matching recess and changes lower guidance. Removing the projection exposes more magnet edge. Retain the specified guide envelope and support its open underside.
